(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[23 1 "// The module _ssl (queue 209, PYS22 (a); CPython 3.14.10's Modules/_ssl.c and its clinic file) over Go's"] [24 1 "// crypto/tls: ssl.py runs unchanged on it. A context (_SSLContext) keeps OpenSSL's settings as _ssl.c reads and"] [25 1 "// writes them (options, verify mode and flags, host flags, the protocol bounds, the cipher list, ALPN, the"] [26 1 "// certificate chain and key, the trust store) and makes a tls.Config of them for each connection. An SSL object"] [27 1 "// (_SSLSocket, over a socket or a pair of MemoryBIOs) drives a tls.Conn in a goroutine of its own over an"] [28 1 "// in-memory transport (builtins_ssl_conn.go), so OpenSSL's non-blocking contract (SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ, a"] [29 1 "// handshake resumed by calling again) holds for both. Verification is _ssl's own over Go's x509 (the codes and"] [30 1 "// messages of OpenSSL's X509_verify_cert_error_string), certificates decoded as _decode_certificate does"] [31 1 "// (builtins_ssl_cert.go). What Go's TLS does not have is by design (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 209\")."] [33 1 "// The constants as CPython 3.14.10 with OpenSSL 3.5 defines them."] [71 2 "// the py_ssl_error codes"] [82 1 "// _ssl.c's line numbers in its error messages (\" (_ssl.c:N)\"), from CPython 3.14.10's source."] [109 1 "// sslReady gives SSLCertVerificationError its two bases (SSLError, ValueError), as egReady does"] [110 1 "// ExceptionGroup's."] [122 1 "// sslError is fill_and_set_sslerror: an exception of type t, its args (code, message), the message"] [123 1 "// \"[LIB: REASON] errstr: verify (_ssl.c:LINE)\" with the parts it has, its reason and library attributes."] [154 1 "// sslPEMLib is OpenSSL's ERR_R_PEM_LIB as _setSSLError reports it."] [159 1 "// ---- the context ----"] [175 30 "// the TLS 1.2-and-below list set_ciphers selected"] [182 35 "// the Python object: an ssl.SSLContext's instance, or the context itself"] [183 35 "// one chain a key type (OpenSSL's SSL_CTX keeps one RSA, one EC ...)"] [188 2 "// queue 552: the PSK callbacks (set_psk_client_callback, set_psk_server_callback) and the server's identity hint"] [197 1 "// sslStoreCert is a certificate of the trust store."] [202 45 "// a fallback root's (x509roots/'s distrust-after)"] [206 46 "// basicConstraints"] [214 46 "// keyUsage's keyCertSign"] [218 2 "// X509_check_ca: a version 1 self-signed certificate is a CA"] [222 1 "// addStore puts a DER certificate in the trust store (once: X509_STORE's hash table)."] [229 11 "// OpenSSL keeps what Go's parser refuses; it cannot anchor Go's verification"] [276 29 "// PY_SSL_MIN_PROTOCOL"] [285 3 "// the subclass's instance made here, so the context knows it (CPython hands the SSLContext itself to the"] [286 3 "// SNI callback and as SSLSocket.context)"] [297 1 "// sslDefaultCiphers is PY_SSL_DEFAULT_CIPHER_STRING."] [300 1 "// tlsVersions is the range of TLS versions the context allows Go: its protocol, its bounds and its OP_NO_*."] [334 1 "// ---- passwords and keys ----"] [336 1 "// sslPassword is a password argument: str, bytes or bytearray (at most PEM_BUFSIZE, 1024 bytes), or a callable"] [337 1 "// called when an encrypted key needs it."] [378 1 "// sslParseKey is a PEM file's first private key, decrypted with the password when it is encrypted."] [387 37 "//nolint: the legacy encryption of OpenSSL's traditional keys"] [426 1 "// ---- the security level (OpenSSL's SSL_CTX_set_security_level) ----"] [428 1 "// sslLevelBits are the security bits each level asks of a key or a signature's digest."] [441 1 "// sslKeyBits is EVP_PKEY_get_security_bits: RSA's by its modulus (BN_security_bits' steps), EC's half its order."] [464 13 "// a key Go reads and OpenSSL rates otherwise (Ed448, ML-DSA): not refused here"] [467 1 "// sslSigBits is X509_get_signature_info's security bits of the certificate's signature digest."] [487 1 "// sslPEMMalformed tells whether a PEM block of the file cannot be decoded (no END line, bad base64): OpenSSL's"] [488 1 "// PEM reader stops there with an error, where Go's pem.Decode skips the block."] [518 16 "// pem.Decode skipped this block for a later one"] [549 2 "// 3.15.2's load_cert_chain: PyErr_SetFromErrnoWithFilename, the file named (queue 263)"] [569 3 "// PEM_read_bio's error on a block it cannot decode, met while SSL_CTX_use_certificate_chain_file reads"] [576 2 "// ssl_security_cert at the context's security level: the leaf's key, then the chain's keys (OpenSSL 3.5"] [577 2 "// refuses no signature digest here: a SHA-1 leaf loads at level 2)"] [722 1 "// sslDefaultPaths are OpenSSL's defaults on Linux, as get_default_verify_paths reports them."] [727 1 "// setDefaultVerifyPaths is X509_STORE_set_default_paths: the default file loaded now, the directory looked up"] [728 1 "// at verification; $SSL_CERT_FILE and $SSL_CERT_DIR replace them. When the host has no store (no certificate in"] [729 1 "// the file, no certificate file in the directories: tamago, a bare container), the checkout's x509roots/ bundle"] [730 1 "// (Mozilla's roots, with their distrust-after dates as constraints) takes its place (the user's decision on"] [731 1 "// 209's DECISION 1, (a), 2026-11-05)."] [787 1 "// SSLRoot is a root of the fallback store: its DER and, when it has one, the constraint a chain it anchors must"] [788 1 "// pass (x509roots/fallback/bundle's Root)."] [794 1 "// sslFallbackRoots is the bundle's roots, set by the package arbace/pyssl (over arbace/x509roots/fallback/bundle),"] [795 1 "// which the interpreted runtime loads the first time it is needed (so a run that verifies against the host's store"] [796 1 "// never loads the bundle's forms) and a compiled program links."] [799 1 "// SetSSLFallbackRoots is arbace/pyssl's registration of the bundle."] [802 1 "// SSLDistrustAfter is the bundle's rule for a root with a distrust-after date: every certificate of the chain"] [803 1 "// issued (NotBefore) on or before it."] [815 1 "// sslFallback is the fallback store's roots: the bundle's, or, for tests, $PYI_SSL_FALLBACK_ROOTS's (a PEM file"] [816 1 "// standing in for the bundle, a block's \"Distrust-After: RFC 3339 time\" header its constraint, as the bundle's"] [817 1 "// distrustAfter)."] [845 1 "// sslX509Roots is _ssl._x509roots(), a test function as _test_decode_cert: the fallback store's roots as"] [846 1 "// (subject, distrust-after) pairs, the date None for an unconstrained root (read back from the constraint's"] [847 1 "// message, the bundle keeping no other trace of it)."] [875 1 "// pool is the trust store as Go's verifier takes it: the store's certificates and those of the capath"] [876 1 "// directories (OpenSSL's by-hash lookup: every certificate file of the directory)."] [906 1 "// ---- ciphers ----"] [908 1 "// sslCipher is a cipher suite Go implements, under OpenSSL's name and attributes."] [912 19 "// SSL_CIPHER_get_version"] [914 19 "// OpenSSL's Kx= and Au= words"] [915 19 "// Enc="] [916 19 "// Mac="] [919 21 "// the cipher-string words that select it"] [928 1 "// sslCiphers are Go's TLS 1.0-1.2 suites in OpenSSL's default order."] [947 2 "// queue 552: the plain PSK suites (RFC 4279, 5487, 7905) of the vendored crypto/tls, offered only with a PSK callback"] [948 2 "// (OpenSSL's ssl_cipher_disabled of kPSK without one)"] [956 1 "// sslIsPSK is a PSK suite (kPSK), offered only with a PSK callback."] [994 1 "// sslSelectCiphers evaluates an OpenSSL cipher string over sslCiphers (ssl_cipher_process_rulestr's operators:"] [995 1 "// ':' ',' ' ' separate, '+' joins words, '!' kills, '-' removes, a leading '+' moves to the end, \"@STRENGTH\","] [996 1 "// \"@SECLEVEL=N\", which may follow a word directly: \"DEFAULT@SECLEVEL=1\"); false when no cipher is selected. level"] [997 1 "// is the last \"@SECLEVEL=N\"'s N, -1 without one."] [1009 2 "// \"DEFAULT\" counts only as the string's first word (ssl_create_cipher_list replaces it by the default list);"] [1010 2 "// a word ends at '@'; a \"@KEYWORD\" ends the item: the rest up to the next separator is skipped, as OpenSSL's"] [1011 2 "// rule parser does (\"HIGH@STRENGTH@SECLEVEL=1\" keeps the level)"] [1083 1 "// sslCipherDict is cipher_to_dict."] [1107 1 "// sslCipherTuple is cipher_to_tuple: (name, protocol, bits)."] [1112 1 "// ---- the module ----"] [1385 19 "// set while the string is read, as OpenSSL's rule parser does"] [1432 3 "// Py_fopen(filepath, \"rb\")'s PySys_Audit(\"open\", \"Osi\", path, mode, 0) (py-small-1127: test_audit's test_open)"] [1443 20 "// Go's TLS has no finite-field DHE: the parameters are read and not used"] [1445 15 "// queue 263: 3.15.2's set_groups and get_groups (_ssl.c, SSL_CTX_set1_groups_list, SSL_CTX_get0_implemented_groups)"] [1462 15 "// OpenSSL 3.3's \"?\": an unknown group ignored"] [1570 2 "// queue 552: _ssl__SSLContext_set_psk_client_callback_impl and _set_psk_server_callback_impl over the vendored crypto/tls"] [1711 35 "// 3.15 (queue 252): TLS 1.3 external PSKs (the vendored crypto/tls, queue 552)"] [1714 2 "// The OpenSSL API level the port follows (ssl.py and the tests branch on it): 3.5.0, the release CPython"] [1715 2 "// 3.14.10's references ran with; the text says what implements it."] [1745 3 "// _ssl.get_sigalgs (3.15, Modules/_ssl.c; queue 252): SSL_get1_builtin_sigalgs split at ':', here the"] [1746 3 "// signature schemes Go's crypto/tls implements, in OpenSSL's names and order"] [1773 20 "// Go's crypto/rand needs no seeding"] [1857 1 "// sslSigalgs is get_sigalgs' answer (3.15; queue 252): the TLS signature schemes of Go's crypto/tls"] [1858 1 "// (defaultSupportedSignatureAlgorithms and the SHA-1 ones it accepts) by OpenSSL 3.5's names, in the order"] [1859 1 "// SSL_get1_builtin_sigalgs lists them."] [1864 1 "// sslGroups are the key exchange groups Go's crypto/tls implements, by OpenSSL 3.5's names in its order"] [1865 1 "// (SSL_CTX_get0_implemented_groups; the NIST curves' aliases P-256, P-384, P-521) (queue 263)."] [1873 1 "// sslGroupIDs are the names set_groups takes for them: OpenSSL's, its aliases and prime256v1, case as OpenSSL's"] [1874 1 "// list matching (x25519 and X25519 both)."] [1886 1 "// sslGroupName is SSL_get0_group_name: the negotiated group's OpenSSL name, None when none."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[206 39] [214 39] [264 53] [278 42] [346 22] [352 49] [354 31] [517 38] [536 53] [545 56] [581 42] [594 40] [642 58] [647 58] [652 26] [663 36] [667 39] [677 35] [698 51] [706 35] [712 33] [734 23] [737 23] [741 32] [749 28] [760 33] [780 58] [819 45] [827 39] [828 45] [863 29] [865 38] [897 48] [1013 51] [1018 36] [1023 41] [1037 56] [1138 41] [1172 24] [1190 24] [1226 106] [1246 88] [1251 88] [1255 90] [1359 23] [1433 60] [1447 40] [1485 35] [1504 29] [1506 38] [1549 30] [1599 15] [1604 41] [1738 28] [1765 29] [1766 36] [1770 32] [1790 33]] :go/trails [[925 113] [953 176] [1680 103] [1695 57] [1706 62]]} (go/file "builtins_ssl.go" :imports [


